## 5. Quick comparison table

| Dimension | GDPR | DPDPA | Operational difference |
|---|---|---|---|
| Form of data covered | Personal data in any form (incl. structured paper filing systems) | Digital personal data only | DPDPA narrower; paper-only records out of scope until digitised |
| Special category regime | Yes (Art. 9) | No statutory regime; subordinate rules may apply via SDF designation | GDPR more prescriptive on sensitive data |
| Extraterritoriality — goods/services | Yes | Yes | Broadly parallel |
| Extraterritoriality — behavioural monitoring | Yes (Art. 3(2)(b)) | No | Major gap; ad-tech / analytics sector materially affected |
| One-Stop-Shop / Lead SA | Yes | No (single national authority) | EU multinationals cannot replicate Irish-style Lead SA structure |
| State / public interest exemption | Member State derogations (Art. 23) | Broad Central Government exemption power (s. 17) | DPDPA more permissive of state exemptions |

