## 6. Open questions and watch items

- **DPDPA Rules on extraterritorial enforcement.** As of the date of this draft, the practical mechanics of enforcing DPDPA against non-Indian data fiduciaries are untested. EU experience (Schrems, Meta, TikTok enforcement) shows that extraterritorial enforcement is possible but resource-intensive; India's Data Protection Board will need to develop similar capability.
- **Treatment of pseudonymised data.** GDPR treats pseudonymised data as personal data (Recital 26). DPDPA does not explicitly address pseudonymisation. Forthcoming Rules or DPB guidance will need to clarify.
- **Interaction with sectoral laws.** Both regimes interact with sectoral laws — financial services, health, telecom — in ways that affect actual scope on the ground. Future chapters will address sectoral overlays.

